  "worked_solution": "The $2$nd row of the matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So, using a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-7 & -1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot {C}_{21}+(-6)\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23}+0\\cdot {C}_{24} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|+(-6)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|-6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
